{"id": "sevt_01BAuTAzyYLy6dMfpNFHSv4K", "content": [{"text": "Checkout p99 went from about 75 ms to about 2,090 ms at 14:09 and kept climbing to about 6,000 ms by 14:59.\n\n- **Deploy:** checkout `0860430` (\"refactor order summary builder for readability\") went out at 14:09:42. The p99 jump is in the 14:09 sample, so the deploy lines up with it. The other deploys don't fit: auth was at 10:47 and cart was at 14:33, after the spike had started.\n- **Diff:** in `CheckoutSummaryHandler.build_summary`, the diff replaces the single batched `order_id IN (...)` query with a loop. The loop runs one `OrderItem` query per open order, which is an N+1 pattern.\n- **Log:** I counted 5,434 per-row queries (`WHERE order_id = ?`) in `app.log`, against 53 batched queries (`order_id IN (?)`). The batched queries are from before the deploy, and the 5,434 per-row queries came after it. I didn't pull per-request query counts or durations.\n\nI didn't check `db_pool_utilization`, since a deploy lined up.\n\n> **Root cause:** `0860430` \u2014 the \"readability\" refactor replaced the single batched `order_items` query with one query per order row (N+1), so each checkout summary now makes many sequential DB round-trips. Reverting it, or restoring the `order_id__in` batch, should fix it.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:54:29.954544Z", "type": "agent.message"}
